15: IS THE NIFTY-RELATIVE FORMULATION BEHAVING AS INTENDED?
==============================================================================
Mathematical fact to verify empirically: relative_momentum[t] = momentum[t] - benchmark_momentum[t]. Since benchmark_momentum[t] is the SAME constant subtracted from every symbol on a given date, subtracting it cannot change the CROSS-SECTIONAL RANK ORDER among a fixed set of symbols -- only the ELIGIBILITY test (>= a floor) can differ, because 'beat NIFTY' and 'positive absolute return' are different conditions whenever NIFTY's own momentum is non-zero.

On the 393 dates where relative-momentum and absolute-momentum eligibility masks agree exactly, rank order matches on 265/266 of them (99.6%) -- confirms ranking itself is (as expected) equivalent; only ELIGIBILITY differs.

Eligibility masks differ on 13.2% of (date, symbol) cells (min_absolute_momentum=0.0 vs min_relative_momentum=0.0 are different conditions whenever NIFTY's own momentum isn't exactly zero).
Selected-set overlap (relative-ranking config vs absolute-ranking config), mean Jaccard: 1.000 -- this is the ACTUAL practical effect of 'use_relative_momentum=True': it changes WHICH names are eligible (via the floor), it does not re-order an otherwise-identical candidate pool.

